# Repository Structure
counterfactual_pitch_sequence_analysis/  
├── data ── stats &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Data for qualified pitchers and batters for each season  

├── data ── pitch_sequence &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; All pitch sequence data for target pitchers by season, downloaded by running ./program/utils/data_downloader.ipynb  

├── data ── pitch_type &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Pitch type data for target pitchers by season, downloaded by running ./program/utils/pitch_type_extractor.ipynb.ipynb  

├── dataset &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Training and testing datasets for Analysis 1 (last pitch) and Analysis 2 (set-up pitch)  

├── model &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; # Folder containing trained Transformer-model and training metadata  

├── program &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; # Program codes for the analysis  

├── program ── utils &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; # Utility programs for setting up the analysis environment, including downloading data, building datasets, and other preparatory tasks  

├── program ── Train_transformer_model.ipynb &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; # Program for hyperparameter search and Transformer model training based on the search results  

├── program ── analysis1.ipynb &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; # Program for performing analysis1. Detailed analysis of the analysis results will be performed using a MATLAB program  

├── program ── analysis2.ipynb &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; # Program for performing analysis2. Detailed analysis of the analysis results will be performed using a MATLAB program  

├── matlab &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; # Folder containing matlab progam for in-depth analysis and visualization of the results. Set this folder in your MATLAB environment.

README.md &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; # This file  

# Installation
This project is designed to be easily run in Google Colab.
All experiments and demonstrations can be reproduced by mounting the project folder and running the main notebooks.

The procedure for reproducing the analyses in this study is as follows:

1. Run the four programs located in `./program/utils` to construct the dataset. Please make sure to run `data_downloader.ipynb` first.

2. Run `Train_transformer_model.ipynb` to train and test the base model. This notebook also includes hyperparameter tuning.

3. Run `analysis1.ipynb` and `analysis2.ipynb` to conduct the analyses described in the paper.

4. Run `analysis1.m` and `analysis2.m` to summarize and visualize the analysis results. Before running these programs, please save the outputs from the corresponding notebooks above in the `./results` folder (generated by the ipynb files) under the names `analysis1` and `analysis2`, respectively.

# Requirements
・Google Colab for the Python environment  
・MATLAB (operation confirmed with R2025b)

